  "content": {
    "title": "Agent observability on the Claude Platform",
    "title_en": "Agent observability on the Claude Platform",
    "summary": "",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "b001",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You can now send OpenTelemetry (OTel) traces from Claude Managed Agents, the Messages API, and Claude SDKs to any OTel tool, and follow each step your agents take. If you already send Claude Code or Cowork traces to your observability tool, the agents you build on the Claude Platform can also show up in the same place."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "b002",
        "type": "heading",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Trace agents with OpenTelemetry"
          }
        ],
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b003",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Trusting an agent with more access starts with tracing its model calls, tool use, and MCP server calls. Review its traces, then widen its access as it proves reliable."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "b004",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Add a destination in the Claude Console, and every agent turn, model call, and tool use arrives in your observability tool as a standard OpenTelemetry trace, with latency, tokens, and IDs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "b005",
        "type": "image",
        "attrs": {
          "url": "https://assets.claude.com/28fe34519808d40faa51162351234a3790230860.png",
          "alt": "How OpenTelemetry traces work"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b006",
        "type": "heading",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Works with your observability tools"
          }
        ],
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b007",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "inlines": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Claude traces follow the "
          },
          {
            "type": "link",
            "attrs": {
              "url": "https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/"
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic conventions"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", so data from Claude and other providers works in the same tools and dashboards."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "b011",
        "type": "list",
        "attrs": {
          "ordered": false
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "b008",
            "type": "list_item",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Debug agents next to the rest of your stack"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". In "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "url": "https://grafana.com/docs/grafana-cloud/observe-and-act/agent-observability/guides/send-claude-platform-traces/"
                },
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Grafana Cloud"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "url": "https://docs.honeycomb.io/send-data/use-cases/claude-platform"
                },
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Honeycomb"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "url": "https://sentry.io/cookbook/trace-claude-platform-with-opentelemetry/"
                },
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Sentry"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", and "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "url": "https://agent-observability-docs.splunk.com/sdk-api/third-party-integrations/claude"
                },
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Splunk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", agent traces sit beside your logs and metrics, so you can see which service a slow or failed step came from."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "b009",
            "type": "list_item",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Improve agents with production data"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". With "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "url": "https://arize.com/docs/ax/integrations/platforms/claude-managed-agents/claude-managed-agents-tracing"
